ding of the narrative)\n    58→\n    59→3. **False character split: James Gatz vs. Gatsby (NEW ISSUE IN ATTEMPT 3)**\n    60→   - Problem: \"James Gatz\" is now listed as a SEPARATE supporting character (6 mentions) with alias \"Mr. Gatz\", while \"Gatsby\" is a main character with alias \"Mr. Gatsby\"\n    61→   - Evidence: **Jay Gatsby** and **James Gatz** are the SAME PERSON - James Gatz is Gatsby's birth name\n    62→   - This is WORSE than attempt 2, where they were at least grouped together (though with inverted primary/alias)\n    63→   - The fix in attempt 3 appears to have OVER-CORRECTED and split them into separate people\n    64→   - Location: Character alias resolution in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py`\n    65→   - **Root cause hypothesis:** The validation logic added in attempt 3 to prevent family member merges may have been too aggressive and is now rejecting valid same-person merges\n    66→   - Fix: Need to ensure \"FirstName LastName\" can merge with \"DifferentFirstName LastName\" ONLY when they are genuinely the same person (birth name vs. adopted name), NOT when they are family members\n    67→   - **Score impact:** -3 points (critical error - these are the same person, not two different people)\n    68→\n    69→### HIGH\n    70→\n    71→4. **Chapter titles still show mixed numbering: \"Chapter 2: II\", \"Chapter 3: III\"**\n    72→   - Problem: Chapter titles append Roman numerals incorrectly: \"Chapter 2: II\" instead of \"Chapter II\" or just \"Chapter 2\"\n    73→   - Evidence: Found 9 chapters (correct count ✓) but titles are malformed\n    74→   - Expected: Either \"Chapter I, Chapter II, ...\" (source format) or \"Chapter 1, Chapter 2, ...\" (normalized), not mixed\n    75→   - Location: Chapter title formatting in `src/pipeline/chapter_detection/consensus.py`\n    76→   - Fix: After selecting the best title from consensus, normalize it - if Roman numerals are detected, format as \"Chapter [Roman]\", not \"Chapter [Arabic