98→   - Expected behavior: Should primarily flag proper nouns (character/place names), genuinely foreign words, archaic terms, homographs\n    99→   - Location: `src/agents/pronunciation_agent.py` or `src/pipeline/pronunciation/`\n   100→   - Fix: Implement better filtering - use dictionary lookup to exclude common English words, focus on proper nouns and genuinely unusual terms\n   101→   - **Score impact:** -3 points (creates noise that obscures genuinely difficult words)\n   102→\n   103→8. **Missing key names in pronunciation guide**\n   104→   - Problem: Important character names like \"Gatsby\" and \"Wolfsheim\" do not appear in the pronunciation guide\n   105→   - Evidence: Searched for both names in pronunciation section - neither appears\n   106→   - Expected: \"Wolfsheim\" especially needs pronunciation guidance (WOLF-shime vs WOLF-sheem)\n   107→   - Location: Pronunciation detection logic\n   108→   - Fix: Ensure all character names from character extraction are automatically included in pronunciation guide\n   109→   - **Score impact:** -2 points (missing critical proper nouns)\n   110→\n   111→### MEDIUM\n   112→\n   113→9. **Jordan Baker profile contains factual error**\n   114→   - Problem: Profile states \"She is involved in a relationship with Tom Buchanan\"\n   115→   - Evidence: Jordan Baker is **not** in a relationship with Tom - she dates **Nick Carraway** (the narrator)\n   116→   - Tom is married to Daisy; the profile appears to confuse the relationships\n   117→   - Location: Character relationship extraction or profile generation\n   118→   - Fix: Improve relationship extraction to correctly parse \"Jordan dates Nick\" vs \"Tom is married to Daisy\"\n   119→   - **Score impact:** -1 point (significant factual error in a main character profile)\n   120→\n   121→10. **No relationships detected**\n   122→    - Problem: \"Key Relationships\" section says \"No explicit relationships detected\"\n   123→    - Evidence: Tom Buchanan and Daisy Buchanan are married (central to plot), Nick and Daisy are cousins, etc.\n   124→    - Location: Relationship extraction in character profiling\n   125→    - Fix: Improve relationship detection to capture family relationships (spouse, cousin, parent, sibling)\n   126→    - **Score impact:** -1 point (reduces utility for narrator preparation)\n   127→\n   128→11. **Plot summary contains minor errors**\n   129→    - Problem: Beyond the critical \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard\" error, there may be other factual issues\n   130→    - Evidence: Haven't fully verified all plot details, but narrator error suggests prompt may be prone to hallucination\n   131→    - Location: Summary generation\n   132→    - Fix: Improve fact-checking or grounding in summaries\n   133→    - **Score impact:** -1 point (in addition to critical #2)\n   134→\n   135→### LOW\n   136→\n   137→12. **Chapter 1 vs. Chapter 5 title inconsistency**\n   138→   - Problem: \"Chapter 1\" and \"Chapter 5\" have plain titles, but others have Roman numerals appended\n   139→   - Evidence: Titles are inconsistent across the document\n   140→   - Location: Chapter title selection logic\n   141→   - Fix: Will be resolved when high issue #4 is addressed\n   142→   - **Score impact:** Included in structure detection score\n   143→\n   144→13. **Common words in \"Foreign Words\" section**\n   145→   - Problem: \"cigarette\" and \"bureau\" listed as foreign words needing pronunciation\n   146→   - Evidence: These are common English words (albeit of French origin) that don't need special guidance\n   147→   - Location: Foreign word detection\n   148→   - Fix: Be more selective about what counts as \"foreign\" - only flag words that maintain foreign pronunciation\n   149→   - **Score impact:** -0.5 points (creates minor noise)\n   150→\n   151→## Detailed Score Justification\n   152→\n   153→### Structure Detection: 5/10\n   154→- **Chapter count correct:** 9 chapters detected (✓ correct!)\n   155→- **Chapter titles malformed:** \"Chapter 2: II\" format (-2 points)\n   156→- **Chapter 4 suspiciously short:** 763 words suggests boundary error (-1 point)\n   157→- **Front matter:** Correctly identified 1 front matter region (+1 point)\n   158→- **Improvement from Attempt 1:** Fixed critical issue (7→9 chapters), but title formatting still broken\n   159→- **Total:** 5/10\n   160→\n   161→### Character Extraction: 2/10\n   162→- **CRITICAL MERGE (UNFIXED):** George Wilson + Myrtle Wilson still merged (-5 points)\n   163→- **NEW CRITICAL SPLIT:** James Gatz and Gatsby are now separate characters (-3 points)\n   164→- **Owl Eyes present:** In supporting characters (OK) (+0.5 points)\n   165→- **Main characters present:** Nick, Daisy, Tom, Jordan, Baker, Wolfshiem detected (+5 points)\n   166→- **Correct distinction:** Tom Buchanan and Daisy Buchanan kept separate (+1 point)\n   167→- **Total:** 10/10 possible, -8 for critical errors = 2/10\n   168→\n   169→### Character Profiles: 6/10\n   170→- **Jordan Baker relationship error:** States she's with Tom instead of Nick (-2 points)\n   171→- **General accuracy:** Most profiles appear factually accurate (+5 points)\n   172→- **Relationships missing:** No relationships extracted (-1 point)\n   173→- **Physical descriptions:** Present but thin (+1 point)\n   174→- **Evidence citations:** Some profiles have source evidence (+3 points)\n   175→- **Total:** 6/10\n   176→\n   177→### Chapter Summaries: 6/10\n   178→- **CRITICAL NARRATOR ERROR:** \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard\" instead of Nick Carraway (-3 points)\n   179→- **Minor plot errors:** Beyond narrator issue (-1 point)\n   180→- **Completeness:** Summaries appear to capture key events (+5 points)\n   181→- **Length:** Appropriate detail for narrator prep (+2 points)\n   182→- **Tone noted:** Summaries indicate mood/atmosphere (+2 points)\n   183→- **Total:** 10/10 possible, -4 for errors = 6/10\n   184→\n   185→### Pronunciation Guide: 4/10\n   186→- **Excessive false positives:** 517 common words flag